Chapter: E1000PhyAbsent
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Kernel chapter E1000e
  cites Kernel chapter Pci

 The refusal half of the PHY path. A model that can only answer is not a
 test of the driver that handles a PHY which does not, and MDIC has two
 distinct ways to fail that a driver can easily fold into one: the MAC
 never reports the transaction ready, and the MAC reports it as an error.
 Its `.vmargs` holds the first, which is a PHY that is not answering at
 all.

 Two things are asserted.

 The read must come back as the error sentinel rather than as zero. Zero
 is a legitimate value for most PHY registers, so a driver that returns
 it on a timeout has thrown the failure away -- which is the same defect
 the reset verdict had at CL 12079, in a different register.

 The bring-up must still leave the device PRESENT. This is deliberate and
 it is the opposite of the reset case: a part whose PHY we cannot reach
 may still bring a link up on its own, so refusing the device outright
 would be worse than trying. What the driver must not do is claim a link
 it never observed, and `link` below is the reading that would catch
 that.

Section: Fixtures

  found-dev : PciScanResult -> Maybe PciDevice
  found-dev (scan) = e1000-find scan

Section: Judges

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

  bar-of : PciDevice -> Integer
  bar-of (dev) =
   let enabled = pci-enable-device dev
   in (pci-parse-bar (dev.pci-bus) (dev.pci-dev) (dev.pci-func) 0).bar-base

  read-is-error : PciDevice -> Boolean
  read-is-error (dev) = e1000-phy-read (bar-of dev) e1000-phy-id1 < 0

  bring-up-answers-zero : PciDevice -> Boolean
  bring-up-answers-zero (dev) = e1000-phy-bring-up (bar-of dev) == 0

  still-present : PciDevice -> Boolean
  still-present (dev) = (e1000-init dev).e-present

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let scan = pci-scan-bus 0
    in act
      when found-dev scan
        is Just (dev) -> act
          print-line-uni ("read is error   : " & yn (read-is-error dev))
          print-line-uni ("bring-up zero   : " & yn (bring-up-answers-zero dev))
          print-line-uni ("still present   : " & yn (still-present dev))
        end
        is None -> print-line-uni ("candidate found : no")
    end
  end

